-- title:
--   Centres of places avoiding all supersingular tubes have non-supersingular j
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5 \le q$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. The arithmetic base is a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `hA : A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. All function fields are subfields of Laurent series fields: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated by the images under coefficientwise extension of the full level-$M'$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`; `fieldBar q M'` is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, the corresponding base change of the $X_H$ function field of level $q^2M'$ for the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ given by the kernel of the reduction map of unit groups; `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is the subfield of Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ generated by the two $j$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC`. A `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ and a principal ideal ring; `Place.ord`, `Place.evalAt` and `Place.IsRational` denote its normalised order function, its residue evaluation through $K$, and the condition that $K$ surjects onto its residue field.
--
--   The hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   (i) Supersingular places of the special fibre: a finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` with `hW` saying that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, the set of places $w$ that are rational, affine geometric, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathtt{jGeomGen}) \in$ `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`.
--
--   (ii) The two function fields are compared by `hle : modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   (iii) Reduction data: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is, a valuation subring `R₀.integers` lying over $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the special-fibre field whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which is compatible with the residue map of $A$, a scaling clause making every nonzero element reducible to something nonzero, and a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors; together with `hR₀`, which says that every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` and has $R_0$-residue the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   (iv) Igusa-component data: a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ (an element of `Idx q`) and a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, subject to: `hIg_inf`, identifying $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ as a Gauss ring, namely $f$ belongs to it iff there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with nonzero reduction of $y$ and $f\cdot y = x$ coefficientwise over $A$; `hIg`, that every line $\ell$ is $\mathrm{redQ}_q(\gamma)\cdot\infty$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, that for every root of unity $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family.
--
--   (v) Supersingular-tube data: a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $W$, subject to: `hSS_A`, that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ iff it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, which states for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` having no poles outside those of $j$ (for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$, where $j$ is the element `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`) and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, that the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and that for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix`, invariance of each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, the existence for each $s$ of an element $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ such that $t - a$ is a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   (vi) A `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q^2*M') (levelH q M')` (the same data as in (iii) without the map on places), with `hR : R.integers = OIg (lineInfty q)`, and `hR₀O`, saying that $f \in$ `R₀.integers` iff its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$.
--
--   (vii) Ramification and constant-field data: an element $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0 \cap A$ such that the contraction of $A$ to $k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), Henselian (`hhens`) and with algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), together with `hκ`, saying that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0 \cap A$; an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity, and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0 \cap A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   (viii) One finite layer of constants: an intermediate field $K_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, finite over $k_0$, and a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ whose elements are exactly those of $K_1$ lying in $A$, assumed to be a discrete valuation ring and a Henselian local ring.
--
--   The conclusion is stated with `fieldBar q M'` regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and asserts the following for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ satisfying four conditions: the constants together with $F_0$ generate everything, i.e. the $k_0$-subfield generated by the range of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'` joined with $F_0$ is $\top$; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\, m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is $K'$-linearly independent and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $k_0(K')$ and $F_0$ with $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$, all $a_i$ vanish; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series has rational coefficients (lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`) belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Fix such an $F_0$, put $F_1$ for the compositum, over $k_0$, of the image of $K_1$ and of $F_0$ inside `fieldBar q M'`, and assume an $A_1$-algebra structure on $F_1$ whose structure map agrees with the inclusions $A_1 \subseteq K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Fix a nonzero $j_1 \in F_1$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the element $j$ of (v), i.e. the inclusion of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`. The relevant geometry is the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ F₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $X_{\mathrm{Fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $F_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $X_{\mathrm{Inf}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along the middle chart, with pushout inclusions `ιFin`, `ιInf` and structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$.
--
--   Four predicates are introduced. For a point $x$ of the model and $f \in F_1$, `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ with `ιFin`-image $x$ there are $g, h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$, and likewise for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Inf}}$ over $x$ with `chartAlgInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$ in both clauses. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational and that for every $f \in F_1$ with `InStalk x f` one has $f \in P$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. Finally `GoodPt x` requires that $x$ map to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$ under `toBase`, that $x$ be closed (any $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$), that for every $y$ of either chart over $x$ every chart element whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of `R.integers` lie in $y$, and that for every $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` with kernel $y$, $\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin}) \notin$ `ssJSet q Ω`; this last predicate is introduced but does not occur in the conclusion.
--
--   The assertion is then: for every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is rational and which lies in no supersingular tube, in the sense that for every $s \in W$ it fails that for all $f \in$ `R₀.integers` having no poles outside those of $j$ and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and all $a \in A$ with residue equal to $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the element $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in $A$ and in its maximal ideal; and for every point $x$ of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ F₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) with `Centred P x`; and for every point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{Fin}}$ whose `ιFin`-image is $x$; and for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin A₁ F₁ j₁` to $\Omega$ with kernel exactly the prime of $y$, one has
--   $$\varphi(\mathtt{jChartFin } A_1\, F_1\, j_1) \notin \mathtt{ssJSet } q\, \Omega,$$
--   where `ssJSet q Ω` is the set of those $j \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j$ has no nonzero affine point killed by $q$.
--
--   This is the converse half of the comparison between supersingular tubes on the level-$q^2M'$ curve and supersingular $j$-invariants on the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of the $j$-line: a rational place avoiding every supersingular tube can only be centred at a point of the model whose $j$-coordinate reduces to a non-supersingular value. It is used in the construction of points of the integral model at which a translate of a given place is centred ([`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_levelAutBar_smul_centred_twoChartIntegralModel_of_forall_not_ssTube)), and it rests on the stalk criterion `inStalk_and_inMax_iff_mem_asIdeal_chartAlg_twoChartIntegralModel` together with `exists_ssTube_of_residue_evalAt_mem_ssJSet`, which produces a supersingular tube containing a place whose $j$-value reduces into `ssJSet`.
